The box model has 4 layes.
--> Margin
--> Border
--> Padding
--> content

Margin is the first layes which give place outside of content, either left or right.
Here is Example: 
margin-top="20px";
margin-left="30px"; / auto;
margin-right="25px"; / auto;
margin-buttom="10px";
Whereas here comes interesting part. When we need content in center of the page, we have to play with margin and make it happen. Here's the code:
margin-left= auto;
margin-right= auto;

Border is the second layer which make border line visible, control thickness of the border.
To make border line visible we can just write:
border=2px solid black;
Here solid black is the color of the border we can change as our need.
border-radius: 100px;
Border-radius make the border line curver and ovel making the corder more soft.

Padding is the third layer, it work similar as margin the writing style is same, we just need to change px and change margin into padding. That's it
It make space for content to breath inside the border line.
We want the content in right side making space in left...
padding-right=0; / padding-left=50px;

Content is the middle part/ last layer which is cover by padding then border then margin.

This model is called box model, because it acts like one.




